### Confirmed finding and fix

Anyone holding a saved calendar’s public `/open/feed/{token}.ics` URL could still receive an event’s title and link after the calendar owner was deactivated. `internal/db/savedsearch.go` ran the feed query as the owner without checking whether that owner could still sign in. The regression test sets the sample Fall Picnic to **pending**, with its deactivated owner as `added_by`; the old code returned `200` with `SUMMARY:Fall Picnic` and its URL.

Before: The token continued to serve that pending event after its owner was deactivated.
Now: The feed returns 404 when the owner fails the existing `Model.SignedIn` check.

The fix is one condition in `savedSearchICS`, using `m.SignedIn(m.addressOf(row["person"]))`. The test is `TestSavedSearchFeedStopsWhenOwnerLeaves` in `internal/db/savedsearch_test.go`. `docs/when/calendar.md` now states when a feed stops. These three files are the only intended changes.

